Part 1 of the RFC isn't in `reef/harness`, so the existing readers in `reef/harness/tasks/trajectory.py` are the likely place for the conversion. I didn't open the artifact-evaluation code, so the last slot is a guess.

The change adds `conversations()` to `reef/core/trajectory_index.py` and makes artifact evaluations use it. The built-in session readers (`HermesSessionReader`, `OpencodeSessionReader`, `DeepseekSessionReader`, `NativeSessionReader`) are the ones that need ATIF conversion. `reef/core/trajectories.py` and `reef/core/atif_payloads.py` look like the ATIF builder, so they may also change.

